        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">Every 40 to 50 hours of use, confirmed by
            the finger test at the centre of the deck.</strong> For most
            households that is quarterly; for a light walker, twice a year; for a
            family of runners, every five or six weeks. Heavier users should
            shorten whichever figure applies by a third.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
            When the answer is yes, the method is in the
            <a href="/treadmill-belt-lubrication/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">lubrication guide</a>
            — one to two ounces of 100 per cent silicone, nothing else — and the
            rest of the year's jobs are in the
            <a href="/treadmill-maintenance/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">maintenance schedule</a>.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
